cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Hexapod CPG — Bio-inspired Locomotion on a Custom 18-DoF Robot"
message: "If you reference this code in academic or industrial work, please cite as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bliss
    given-names: Jangara
abstract: >-
  A four-person Fort Lewis College team's 18-DoF hexapod for NASA Space
  Grant's Colorado Robotics Challenge, plus a later Python central pattern
  generator (CPG) simulator. The repository holds the chassis CAD (derived
  from Mark W's open-source skeleton), Arduino-Mega firmware extended from
  Mark W's original with IMU heading hold and bump avoidance, and the CPG
  simulator: six Kuramoto-coupled phase oscillators whose target phase
  offsets blend from a wave to a tripod pattern as the natural frequency
  rises, driving an 18-DoF inverse-kinematics model, with a 34-test suite.
  The CPG runs in simulation only.
keywords:
  - robotics
  - hexapod
  - central-pattern-generator
  - kuramoto
  - coupled-oscillators
  - gait-generation
  - inverse-kinematics
  - arduino
  - imu
  - bioinspired-robotics
